Local fix, not yet reported upstream (netcdf-c 4.9.3, libhdf5/hdf5open.c).

read_coord_dimids() reads the hidden _Netcdf4Coordinates attribute of a
multi-dimensional coordinate variable into var->dimids, an array of
var->ndims C ints, but passes the attribute's own *file* datatype
(H5Aget_type) as the memory type. A corrupt file that declares the
attribute with a wider element type (8-byte integers, or an array or
compound type) therefore makes H5Aread write npoints * sizeof(file type)
bytes into a buffer of npoints * sizeof(int): a heap-buffer-overflow in
H5A__read reached by nc_open of an untrusted UGRID/netCDF-4 file.

netCDF itself writes this attribute as H5T_NATIVE_INT, so reading it with
H5T_NATIVE_INT is the intended contract: HDF5 converts a valid file's
values unchanged, and an attribute type that cannot convert to an int
makes H5Aread fail, which the function already reports as NC_EATTMETA.
Remove the patch once the pinned netCDF release reads it this way.

--- a/libhdf5/hdf5open.c
+++ b/libhdf5/hdf5open.c
@@ -330,7 +330,7 @@ read_coord_dimids(NC_GRP_INFO_T *grp, NC_VAR_INFO_T *var)
         BAIL(NC_EATTMETA);
 
     /* Read the dimids for this var. */
-    if (H5Aread(coord_attid, coord_att_typeid, var->dimids) < 0)
+    if (H5Aread(coord_attid, H5T_NATIVE_INT, var->dimids) < 0)
         BAIL(NC_EATTMETA);
     LOG((4, "read dimids for this var"));
 
